// gnn/ — graph neural networks: message passing, pooling and read-out.
//
// `message_passing.mbt` is the centre of this package rather than an
// afterthought. Gilmer et al. (2017) showed every GNN is three steps at every
// node -- aggregate, update, read out -- and eleven files here are written
// against that interface rather than against a specific architecture. Putting
// it anywhere else would leave those eleven depending on it through the root.
//
// `gradient_check.mbt` comes along for a plainer reason: it has no dependencies
// outside this package and the only two files that use it are the two GNN
// gradient gates.
//
// The circular pair noted during the dependency survey -- gat_stack_backward
// reaching gnn_paramcheck, which reaches back -- is internal to this package,
// so it costs nothing. Splitting on a prefix would have split the pair in half.
//
// rl/ is imported by three files, and it is a real dependency rather than a
// convenience: Set2Set and graph attention both read out node sets with an
// LSTM, iterating the attention to convergence rather than pooling in one
// pass. That is an RNN doing attention, so graph attention lives downstream of
// the recurrent package.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/nn",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/neuron",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/rl",
}
